@startuml
title Delivery: the groundness switch, and the ordering hazard it opens

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam activity {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
  BorderColor #9CA3AF
}

start

:the search delivers entries
""[ step_0, …, step_{k-1}, leaf ]"";
note right #DBEAFE
  The ENTRY SHAPE does not change.
  It is already the FIPS's, already
  ""deliver""'s, already the codec's
  split-eligible form.
end note

if (which ""LeafProjection""?) then ([RestingOn]\nover a data-term guest)
  #DCFCE7:leaf is an ""EList""/""ETuple""
  of ground literals;
  #DCFCE7:**GROUND**
  ""eval_stable_par"" admits it;
  note right #DCFCE7
    This is the FIPS's headline use case.
    It gets ""serialized_paths"": canonical
    identity, NO producer sort obligation,
    and wire-level prefix structure.
  end note
  #DCFCE7:""combine_epathmap"" canonicalises
  to **TRIE ORDER**;
else ([Configuration]\nor a truncated branch)
  #FEF3C7:leaf is a REIFIED PROCESS
  (""reify"" output, or
  ""(handle, frontier, ⟦config⟧)"");
  #FEF3C7:**NOT GROUND**
  it carries sends/receives/
  free variables;
  #FEE2E2:⚠ ""combine_epathmap"" then
  **PRESERVES ENTRY ORDER**
  — branch enumeration order
  becomes OBSERVABLE;
  note right #FEE2E2
    **THE ONE THING THAT WOULD SILENTLY
    BREAK CONSENSUS.** Today ""deliver""
    avoids it by using ""ESet"", because
    ""ParSet"" sorts and is therefore canonical.
  end note
  #DCFCE7:**FIX** — producer-side ordering:
  sort each entry with ""ParSortMatcher"",
  build the trie over the SORTED entries,
  read back in trie order;
  note right #DCFCE7
    Zero consensus change.
    ⚠ The trie must be built over the
    SORTED entries — sorting can change
    an entry, and therefore its key.
  end note
endif

#EDE9FE:three maps, never merged
""success"" · ""truncated"" · ""failure""
<i>they differ in GROUNDNESS, and a union
would be non-ground whenever any member is</i>;

#FCE7F3:gate: ""x8_publication_is_scheduler_invariant""
must be run against the new shape before merge;

stop

@enduml
